 "summary": "The new public theorem states the classical spatial H\u00f6lder estimate for the Duhamel Hessian: the constant is chosen before the forcing, time and bounds, so it is independent of `t` and `M`, and the hypotheses are measurability, an a.e. bound and a.e. H\u00f6lder slices, none of which build in the conclusion. The power-splitting integral lemma is correct, its hypotheses can be met, and it holds in both cases `t \u2264 d` and `t > d`.",
